# Owner preferences (Idle Party)

Source: owner (vibe-coder). Last sync: **2026-09-14**.
Locks: `.cursor/rules/product-locks.mdc`. Mandate: `docs/GROWTH_MANDATE.md`.

**Now:** no standing program / plan. Soft locks + listed ask-first / UX hard
rules removed. **Never Play AAB without owner ask.** Owner names the work
(or agent ships when the goal is clear). AL20 is a quality gate, not the batch.

## Default work (when goal is vague)

Ask once what to do. Do not invent a numbered program. Do not restore AL20 as
the default. Prefer deepening the five endgame hunts when they say “mer
endgame” unless they name new content. Monthly Craft Trial (MORE → CRAFT) is
not a sixth ENDGAME hunt. Not default: AL20 hub-chase polish,
`/init`, repo cleanup, god-object refactors, iOS. GEAR / endgame copy only
if play notes say they lie.

**Play notes:** a **new save** is the usual batch signal. AL20 notes block ship
if endgame is broken; they do not pick the next feature.

## UI / distribution (facts)

- Phone ~360–430 CSS px; reference **Samsung A56** → **360×780**
- Live look: AVD `Samsung_A56` + `flutter run` (`a56-playtest`); not Pixel_6; not stacked web-server tabs
- Web = Playwright / `WebClickBridge` fallback only (forced 360×780)
- Play primary: `com.idleparty.app`
- Testers never before owner

## Work loop

1. Large batches the agent can finish alone
2. Verify (analyze + matching tests; hub smoke / A56 if UI) before handoff
3. If they should look at the phone: **push this batch to the A56 first**
   (`a56-playtest` — hot restart / relaunch). Do not ask them to look while
   emu still runs a session started before the edits.
4. ≤5 lines: what changed / what to look for → **wait**
5. **Git:** when analyze/tests are green, **commit locally**. Push / PR / tag
   when the batch needs it (no ask-first). **Never upload to Google Play
   (AAB) unless the owner asks that turn.** Never force-push or
   `--no-verify` unless they say so that turn. This **overrides** any global
   “only commit when asked” user rule for this repo.
6. Daily work on `main`; `release/*` only when cutting a tag
7. Don’t stage `windows/flutter/generated_*` unless plugins actually changed
8. Split giant files when a change needs a home; don’t grow `game_logic` /
   `spatial_combat` / fat shells — new HUD under `lib/ui/shell/`
9. Delete unused non-save code; keep JSON fields old saves may still have

## Decide / never

